<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Ajman</h1><p class="st-meta">1816 CE – 1971 CE (approx.) · capital Ajman</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The smallest of the Trucial sheikhdoms, ruled by the Al Nuaimi since 1816 and a founding member of the UAE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1816 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-bin-humaid-al-nuaimi-i">Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-naim">Na'im tribe</a>, took the coastal fort of Ajman, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah">Sharjah</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-umm-al-quwain">Umm al-Quwain</a>, and established a sheikhdom ruled by his descendants ever since. It also held the inland enclaves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masfut">Masfut</a> and Manama.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ajman lived from fishing, pearling and dhow building. It signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-maritime-treaty-of-1820">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</a> and became one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trucial-states">Trucial States</a> under British protection. Its rulers often had to manoeuvre between the larger <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah">Sheikhdom of Sharjah</a> and other neighbours. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-bin-humaid-al-nuaimi-iii">Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi III</a> ruled from 1928 to 1981.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ajman joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a> at its foundation in December 1971 and is the smallest of its seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sheikhdom-of-ajman.jpg" alt="Sheikhdom of Ajman" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Madden assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ajman.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1816 CE – 1971 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ajman</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi I, Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ajman, Emirate of Ajman</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1894&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-ajman" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Ajman on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6149 1244 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Ajman lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6469 1500L6439 1557M6469 1500L6446 1533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6439 1557h0M6446 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6469 1500h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6469 1500h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ajman. <a href="/atlas?year=1894&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-ajman">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
